From: AOSP RK3576 Baseline <uhf-platform@localbuild>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 08:58:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] uhf: add wire-protocol codec and session arbitration core
 (Phase 1)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Implements UHF-SRS-001 (Rev B) Phase 1's hardware-independent core, kept
deliberately separate from AIDL/Binder plumbing so it is unit-testable on
the host without a framework build or reader hardware:

- UhfProtocol: CRC16, frame build/parse with FR-LNK-03/04/06 resync and
  reCmd matching, the §5.5 status->error mapping, the 0x21 identify decode
  (FR-INF-01..03), the §4.4 band-formula table, and multi-frame inventory
  assembly + tag-record decode (FR-INV-02/03/10). Implements TST-U-01..08
  from the SRS's own test plan plus additional edge cases (fuzzed random
  input, CRC-corrupted-frame stall recovery, truncated/malformed payloads).
  One real bug found via testing and fixed: a CRC-corrupted byte can look
  like a plausible oversized length prefix, stalling scan() forever on a
  closed stream with no more bytes coming; added scanWithStallRecovery()
  to pair frame recovery with FR-LNK-05's inter-byte timeout instead of
  leaving that pairing as an implicit, easy-to-miss caller responsibility.

- UhfTransport: the interface UhfSessionArbiter programs against, so the
  Phase 1 JNI transport and the eventual Phase 2 HAL proxy are swappable
  without touching arbitration policy (SRS §3.2's HAL-split boundary).

- UhfSessionArbiter: session exclusivity and crash recovery (FR-LC-03/04),
  the unconditional boot-time real-time-mode reset and region reassertion
  (FR-LC-05/09), the antenna-check interlock ordering (FR-ANT-02), the RF
  power safety ceiling (FR-PWR-02/03), and the streaming/buffered mutual
  exclusion with auto-restart (FR-STR-08/13, FR-BUF-07) added in SRS Rev B.

65/65 tests pass, compiled and run standalone against junit-4.12 (host
JDK 11, no Android framework/AOSP build required for this layer).

Not yet done: AIDL (IUhfService/IUhfTagCallback/IUhfStateCallback), the
UhfManager/UhfSession client API, UhfService's Binder wrapper around this
arbiter, the JNI serial transport, and the Context/PackageManager/
SystemServiceRegistry/SystemServer/AndroidManifest edits from SRS §8.1.

